---
title: Code Splitting
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code splitting and lazy loading is a powerful technique for improving the bundle size and load performance of an application."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reduces the amount of code that needs to be loaded on initial page load"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code is loaded on-demand when it is needed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Results in more chunks that are smaller in size that can be cached more easily by the browser."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-does-tanstack-router-split-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How does TanStack Router split code?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router separates code into two categories:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Critical Route Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The code that is required to render the current route and kick off the data loading process as early as possible."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path Parsing/Serialization"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Search Param Validation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loaders, Before Load"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route Context"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Data"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Links"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scripts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Styles"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All other route configuration not listed below"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Non-Critical/Lazy Route Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - The code that is not required to match the route, and can be loaded on-demand."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route Component"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Component"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pending Component"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not-found Component"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧠 "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why is the loader not split?"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The loader is already an asynchronous boundary, so you pay double to both get the chunk "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and"}]},{"type":"text","value":" wait for the loader to execute."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Categorically, it is less likely to contribute to a large bundle size than a component."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The loader is one of the most important preloadable assets for a route, especially if you're using a default preload intent, like hovering over a link, so it's important for the loader to be available without any additional async overhead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Knowing the disadvantages of splitting the loader, if you still want to go ahead with it, head over to the "},{"type":"link","href":"#data-loader-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Loader Splitting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"encapsulating-a-route-s-files-into-a-directory","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Encapsulating a route's files into a directory"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since TanStack Router's file-based routing system is designed to support both flat and nested file structures, it's possible to encapsulate a route's files into a single directory without any additional configuration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To encapsulate a route's files into a directory, move the route file itself into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".route"},{"type":"text","value":" file within a directory with the same name as the route file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, if you have a route file named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":", you would create a new directory named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"},{"type":"text","value":" and move the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" file into that directory, renaming it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts.tsx"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route.tsx"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"approaches-to-code-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approaches to code splitting"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router supports multiple approaches to code splitting. If you are using code-based routing, skip to the "},{"type":"link","href":"#code-based-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code-Based Splitting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" section."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you are using file-based routing, you can use the following approaches to code splitting:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#using-automatic-code-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using automatic code-splitting ✨"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#using-the-lazytsx-suffix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#using-virtual-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Virtual Routes"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-automatic-code-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using automatic code-splitting✨"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the easiest and most powerful way to code split your route files."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"autoCodeSplitting"},{"type":"text","value":" feature, TanStack Router will automatically code split your route files based on the non-critical route configuration mentioned above."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"important","title":"Important","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The automatic code-splitting feature is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ONLY"}]},{"type":"text","value":" available when you are using file-based routing with one of our "},{"type":"link","href":"../routing/file-based-routing.md#getting-started-with-file-based-routing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"supported bundlers"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nThis will "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOT"}]},{"type":"text","value":" work if you are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"only"}]},{"type":"text","value":" using the CLI ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/router-cli"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To enable automatic code-splitting, you just need to add the following to the configuration of your TanStack Router Bundler Plugin:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackRouter } from '@tanstack/router-plugin/vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackRouter({\n      // ...\n      autoCodeSplitting: true,\n    }),\n    react(), // Make sure to add this plugin after the TanStack Router Bundler plugin\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That's it! TanStack Router will automatically code-split all your route files by their critical and non-critical route configurations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want more control over the code-splitting process, head over to the "},{"type":"link","href":"./automatic-code-splitting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic Code Splitting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide to learn more about the options available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-the-lazy-tsx-suffix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are not able to use the automatic code-splitting feature, you can still code-split your route files using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix. It is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"as easy as moving your code into a separate file with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLazyFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" function instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"important","title":"Important","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__root.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" route file, using either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRootRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRootRouteWithContext"},{"type":"text","value":", does not support code splitting, since it's always rendered regardless of the current route."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These are the only options that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLazyFileRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" supports:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Export Name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component to render for the route."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorComponent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component to render when an error occurs while loading the route."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingComponent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component to render while the route is loading."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The component to render if a not-found error gets thrown."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"example-code-splitting-with-lazy-tsx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example code splitting with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you are using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":", you can split your route into two files to enable code splitting:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before (Single File)"}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n  component: Posts,\n})\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n  component: Posts,\n})\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  loader: fetchPosts,\\n  component: Posts,\\n})\\n\\nfunction Posts() {\\n  // ...\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  loader: fetchPosts,\\n  component: Posts,\\n})\\n\\nfunction Posts() {\\n  // ...\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After (Split into two files)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This file would contain the critical route configuration:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\n  loader: fetchPosts,\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  loader: fetchPosts,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\nimport { fetchPosts } from './api'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  loader: fetchPosts,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the non-critical route configuration going into the file with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".lazy.tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/posts')({\n  component: Posts,\n})\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/posts')({\n  component: Posts,\n})\n\nfunction Posts() {\n  // ...\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  component: Posts,\\n})\\n\\nfunction Posts() {\\n  // ...\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.lazy.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createLazyFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createLazyFileRoute('/posts')({\\n  component: Posts,\\n})\\n\\nfunction Posts() {\\n  // ...\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"using-virtual-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Virtual Routes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You might run into a situation where you end up splitting out everything from a route file, leaving it empty! In this case, simply "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"delete the route file entirely"}]},{"type":"text","value":"! A virtual route will automatically be generated for you to serve as an anchor for your code split files. This virtual route will live directly in the generated route tree file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before (Virtual Routes)"}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"files"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"file-0","data-tab-index":"0"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { cr